Create these files on the AI-PC with mode 0600; never commit them:

```sh
mkdir -p deploy/aidev/secrets
for name in gateway-jwt runtime-token user01-runtime-key user02-runtime-key user03-runtime-key; do
  openssl rand -hex 32 > "deploy/aidev/secrets/$name"
  chmod 600 "deploy/aidev/secrets/$name"
done
```

The gateway key signs the external session. Each runtime key is unique to one
CloudCLI container, so a token for one environment cannot authenticate to
another. The `runtime-token` is only the internal gateway-to-runtime-manager
credential.
